   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Hello World - Your First React Component
",
    "
",
    "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. The simplest React component is a function that returns JSX (JavaScript XML).
",
    "JSX looks like HTML but is actually JavaScript.
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "hello-world-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "function HelloWorld() {
",
    "  return <h1>Hello, React world!</h1>;
",
    "}
",
    "
",
    "// Render the component
",
    "console.log('Component created: HelloWorld');
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "jsx-markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. JSX and JavaScript Expressions
",
    "
",
    "JSX allows you to embed JavaScript expressions using curly braces `{}`. You can use variables, perform calculations, and call functions inside JSX.
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "jsx-code",
